summary: rust-keylime#1225 - agent must unwrap OCTET-STRING-wrapped EK cert before sending it to the registrar
description: |
    Some hardware TPMs store the EK certificate in NV RAM wrapped in an ASN.1
    OCTET STRING (tag 0x04) instead of a raw DER SEQUENCE (tag 0x30), following
    a convention mentioned in the TCG EK Credential Profile. The rust agent used
    to forward these bytes verbatim and older registrars could not parse them
    (see keylime/keylime#1891 and keylime/rust-keylime#1225).

    This test reconfigures the swtpm emulator so that the EK certificate stored
    in TPM NV RAM is OCTET-STRING wrapped. It backs up and modifies the swtpm
    systemd unit so that swtpm_setup uses a custom create_certs_tool that wraps
    the EK certificate produced by swtpm_localca; swtpm_setup then stores those
    wrapped bytes in the EK certificate NV index.

    It then starts the agent behind an ncat relay that captures the registration
    payload the agent sends to the registrar. The primary check verifies that the
    ekcert the agent puts on the wire is a plain X.509 certificate (starts with
    the SEQUENCE tag 0x30), i.e. the agent unwrapped the OCTET STRING before
    sending. This single on-the-wire check covers both known unfixed failure
    modes: an agent that forwards the wrapped bytes verbatim (capture starts with
    the OCTET STRING tag 0x04), and an agent that fails to parse the wrapped cert
    and registers with "ekcert": null (nothing captured, as observed with
    keylime-agent-rust 0.2.10). As a secondary diagnostic the test also checks
    that the agent log is free of the ASN.1 "wrong tag" parse error emitted by
    the latter.
contact: Karel Srot <ksrot@redhat.com>
component:
  - keylime
test: ./test.sh
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - nmap-ncat
  - python3
  - tpm2-tools
  - openssl
  - coreutils
  - policycoreutils-python-utils
recommend:
  - keylime
  - keylime-agent-rust
duration: 10m
enabled: true
id: f1c2a3d4-5b6e-4f70-8a91-2c3d4e5f6a7b

adjust:
  - when: swtpm is not defined
    enabled: false
    because: This test needs the swtpm emulator to store a wrapped EK cert in NV RAM

  - when: arch == s390x or arch == ppc64le
    enabled: false
    because: EK certificate tooling is limited on these architectures (see setup/configure_tpm_emulator)
